by grep (pcc2_genctl is only a struct field in the guest). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — PASS 13 (Agent; chose reading over building because two panels&#x27; seats were on the machine).  Re-derived all eight part-13 scores from the handler and probe source, name for name.  Two in-rule gaps in the pass-13 repair: L2-a the generating set is ONE-SIDED at the two new (label, INT set, own count 0) cells -- `grep ST_B(13&#x27; finds exactly two sessions and each is followed by ONE wide write, 0x0013, so `&amp;&amp; (idata &amp; ICLR)&#x27;, `&amp;&amp; (idata &amp; 0xe0)&#x27;, `&amp;&amp; !(idata &amp; IEN)&#x27; crossed with the cell escape 251/251 by construction (six shapes); L2-b the INT axis was not crossed with the OTHER count -- (T2, p2=0, INT set, p1&gt;0) and its mirror are reachable pure-state cells `pendboth&#x27; never builds (it has no byte write).  L4: F2 item 6&#x27;s correction was itself arithmetically false -- 0x10 &amp; ~0xf0 == 0, acc all trips TxCTL&#x27;s &amp; ~7 and PSCALEADJ&#x27;s print only (APPLIED).  Item 15&#x27;s stated rejection reason (&#x27;t is a judgment input&#x27;) false -- t is the body&#x27;s longest conjunction; the real grounds are cost (seven binary axes at TxICR -&gt; tens of pty cells per arm) and occurs-vs-observed (APPLIED to CHANGELOG + carrier).  Item 1&#x27;s corrected grading RIGHT, confirmed by a second route (the 242-row figures re-derived: 241/242 and 236/242).  Enumeration verified against all twelve bodies: matches.  The docstring straddle VERIFIED by diff (one hunk, docstring).  Prescribed the pass-14 diff: 0x0000/0x0020/0x0018 (ICLR last) at each new cell; the other-count mirror in pendboth (T2 first) + one new T1-first session; the closed product written into the contract.  Census lesson: sibling parity over rows that WRITE at the arm, not rows NAMED for it. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — PASS 13 (GPT-6 Astra, max; pointer-fed, 448 KB stream).  Zero newly identified runtime defects in the twelve blocks and the helper; coverage finding: an incomplete adopted floor -- the two missing stable TxICR cells, generating-set obligations completed consistently (incl. the TxCTL 0xfc fixture cell -- DISCLOSED as debt: the count classes are not body-tested partitions under the adopted floor), the record corrected: stale &#x27;the first of four wide writes&#x27; texts (pend2/pend1 nine wide writes, pendboth eight -- carried to pass 14), &#x27;not constructible by a probe&#x27; overstates (any of the seven reasserting arms sets INT, not only DEVICE_TICK -- carried), the working diff is comment + typedef not comment-only (the brief&#x27;s text; the CHANGELOG had it right), appended execution can change `alive&#x27; which the rb4 rows consult (true; disclosed).  Valid measured zero: 0 surviving of 7 mutants on 251 rows -- &#x27;does not establish complete floor coverage&#x27;. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — UNKNOWN — Reserved for measurement (owner ruling 2026-08-30); not a seat failure. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — MANUAL — PASS 13 (grok-4.6 xhigh, --prompt-file; 13.6 KB).  Found the two gaps independently: &#x27;Denominator I did not find closed: generating set at the two new floor cells (IEN-clear / ICLR-set / HUH?-set as wide writes); sticky-INT x other-pending.  A zero that does not list those is zero looked for.&#x27;  Grades them L1 on uncommitted detector material -- ADOPTED as the grading (nothing shipped since b78bb0f).  Also confirmed mut_syntax.py&#x27;s hardcoded anchor as a real check-that-cannot-fail and mut_syntax2.py as the right replacement. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — [ollama_kimi.txt] TRANSPORT kimi-k3:cloud (SUBSTITUTE, fired as OLLAMA4 beside the CLI on this date -- two transports for one seat; the CLI&#x27;s own entry is separate).  PASS 13 (packet-fed substitute; the CLI answered too -- two transports for one seat on this date, recorded by transport; OLLAMA4 blanked after this panel).  6.7 KB.  Close; caught that &#x27;0x0001 is HUH?-clear at these arms&#x27; is false at VECBASE (0x0001 &amp; ~0xf0 = 0x01) -- L4 applied to the CHANGELOG and carrier. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — PASS 13 (glm-5.3:cloud, packet-fed).  TWO THINKING BURNS on the 17 KB three-question packet (response empty, done_reason stop, 118-124 KB thinking; kept as ollama_glm.burn.txt / .burn2.txt) -- the fifth seat-failure class, cure as documented: a 2 KB ONE-question packet (brief_pcc2_p13.glm_mini.md) answered on the third firing: (a) INSIDE the floor -- pass 14 is owed (clause 2 is a per-cell requirement); (b) not settleable from the packet.  Recorded as answered on a NARROWER brief than the roster&#x27;s. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — PASS 13 (deepseek-v4-pro:cloud, packet-fed, 2.8 KB).  Objected that the M_ZINT guard `!((reg &amp; INT) &amp;&amp; p == 0 &amp;&amp; label)&#x27; &#x27;is false in that state so it cannot land the write&#x27; -- REJECTED: the guard being false is exactly the case where the decline is skipped and the write LANDS (measured 0x33).  Right that F2 item 1 named two of seven red rows -- L4 applied. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — PASS 13 (minimax-m3:cloud, packet-fed, 7.4 KB).  Chain can close from the packet; one wording defect in premise 3.  Superseded on closure by the file-reading seats&#x27; derivation. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">lcabadval</span><span class="ttl">dev_lca.c: SIX chipset registers in DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc) kill the host on a value outside a small accepted set (CONF, TB_ENA, W_BASE0/1, W_MASK0/1) -- plus a seventh exit in the default arm, which this round does NOT close</span><span class="tip">dev_lca.c: SIX chipset registers in DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc) kill the host on a value outside a small accepted set (CONF, TB_ENA, W_BASE0/1, W_MASK0/1) -- plus a seventh exit in the default arm, which this round does NOT close — witness: harness:ENUMERATED from the shipped source, 2026-08-31.  Eleven live terminating calls.  The value guards, each ending in exit(1): `idata &amp; ~1` (:206), `idata &amp; ~IOC_TB_ENA_TEN` (:226), `idata != 0ULL &amp;&amp; idata != 0x300800000ULL` (:241), `idata != 0x700000ULL` (:256), `idata != 0x240000000ULL` (:280), `idata != 0x3ff00000ULL` (:295).  Each diagnostic says so in its own words -- *&quot;(0x%&quot; PRIx64&quot;) from the only implemented value&quot;*.  Plus two range guards that also kill: `dev &gt;= 21` (:129) and `ofs &gt; len` (:163).  NO rung-3 witness: READ, not booted. — note: *** RECORDS CORRECTION 2026-09-06, from RE-DERIVING this row&#x27;s own citations instead of trusting them.  THE
