D_FMT + TOC_SHORT, counting the #489 TOC diagnostic; its channel is a latch OTHER THAN the one Site A owns, which is exactly why all 20 shipped rows were blind.  The two-site row = BAD_CMD + BAD_FMT: both existing two-site rows fix FMT-then-CMD, where `warned` is 0 at Site A, so a widened guard is indistinguishable -- ONE REVERSED SESSION covers the whole order-asymmetry class.  *** RENAME BEFORE SHIPPING: the seat&#x27;s own name `both sites rev` is exactly 14 chars = the gate&#x27;s column width, so it renders with a trailing space and the gate anchor would miss it.  Use `rev sites`.  The seat found this by noticing its own summary table printed blank for that row while the FAIL list caught it. ***  NOT added to #490: E2/E3 were adjudicated coverage debt rather than floor breaches, and 20 -&gt; 22 rows moves every score in a 13-build table.  More witnesses create more candidate ROUNDS, never bigger rounds. — evidence: [panel_20260829_133206]  measured, supp_p2_20260829/probe_{base,E2_assignA,E3_widenA}.log</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td cl