codex
The lane guard is inconsistent with the indexing: it admits `ofs == len`, which the write path wraps to byte zero and the read path cannot place in the result. I also found that writes forward the nested memory result while reads discard it. I’m checking the memory dispatcher before calling that an uninitialized-data defect.
