codex
The fork already zeroes read buffers for failed translations and device reads, so the uninitialized-byte claim needs a narrower argument than the filed summary gives. I also found a separate issue: the bridge passes its physical ISA address with `CACHE_NONE`, which does not bypass Alpha address translation. I’m checking that dependency and the existing test coverage.
