web search: 
web search: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NetBSD/src/trunk/sys/arch/alpha/pci/lca_bus_io.c
codex
None of the inspected regressions exercises the sparse `lca_isa` handler. The IRQ probe accesses the downstream ISA mapping directly; the other LCA probes cover configuration registers. I also confirmed a narrow exception to buffer zeroing: the halt-on-unmapped-memory path returns before filling the byte, although the outer dispatcher then suppresses CPU writeback. That does not support the filed claim of a general guest-visible uninitialized read.
